        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Mind-Body Problem: Historical Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "STARTING POINT: Methodological doubt.\n  What can I know with certainty?\n  I can doubt the external world.\n  I can doubt my body.\n  But can I doubt that I am thinking, right now, as I doubt?\n  NO. Cogito ergo sum: \"I think, therefore I am.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md#008",
      "path": [
        "01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:philosophy-of-mind:01-mind-body-problem, git-history:philosophy-of-mind:01-mind-body-problem]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophy-of-mind/01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md",
        "concepts": "[mind, body, problem]",
        "current_path": "philosophy-of-mind/01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md",
        "id": "maxim:philosophy-of-mind:mind-body-problem",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "philosophy-of-mind",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[mind, body]",
        "section": "philosophy-of-mind",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Mind-Body Problem: Historical Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CONSEQUENCE:\n  My existence as a thinking thing is certain.\n  My body's existence can be doubted.\n  Therefore: I (the thinking thing) am distinct from my body.\n  Mind (res cogitans -- thinking substance) is distinct from\n  body (res extensa -- extended substance)."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md#009",
      "path": [
        "01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md"
      ],
