        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Mind-Body Problem: Historical Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Physical causation: requires spatial contact, forces, mechanisms.\n  Non-physical mind has no spatial location.\n  Therefore: how?"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md#014",
      "path": [
        "01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:philosophy-of-mind:01-mind-body-problem, git-history:philosophy-of-mind:01-mind-body-problem]",
        "canonical_path": "philosophy-of-mind/01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md",
        "concepts": "[mind, body, problem]",
        "current_path": "philosophy-of-mind/01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md",
        "id": "maxim:philosophy-of-mind:mind-body-problem",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "philosophy-of-mind",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[mind, body]",
        "section": "philosophy-of-mind",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Mind-Body Problem: Historical Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DESCARTES' ANSWER: The pineal gland.\n  A small gland at the center of the brain.\n  Descartes thought it was the unique unpaired structure.\n  (Wrong -- it's not; but this was 17th century anatomy.)\n  The soul is \"closely joined\" to the pineal gland.\n  Fluid in the brain's ventricles transmits soul's intentions to body."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md#015",
      "path": [
        "01-MIND-BODY-PROBLEM.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:philosophy-of-mind:01-mind-body-problem, git-history:philosophy-of-mind:01-mind-body-problem]",
