        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "The Mind-Body Problem: Historical Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "PRINCESS ELIZABETH'S CHALLENGE (1643):\n  Descartes corresponded with Princess Elizabeth of Bohemia.\n  She pressed him: how can an unextended substance exert force\n  on a body, as all force requires contact and area?\n  Descartes had no satisfactory answer.\n  This remains the core problem.\n```"
    }
